\begin{align*} \langle -1, 3 \rangle \cdot \langle 1, 5 \rangle = 15-1 &= \sqrt{10}\sqrt{26}\cos(\theta),\\ \implies \cos (\theta) &= \frac{7}{\sqrt{65}}. \end{align*}
Thus, \[\tan(\angle ABC) = \sqrt{\frac{65}{49}-1}= \boxed{\frac{4}{7}}.\]

